# {{.Name}}

A Caja **static-page** project — `main.caja` runs once at build time and writes
plain HTML/CSS into `dist/` via the `page` builtin module, the same way a
static site generator's build step works.

## Development

```
caja serve
```

Builds the project and serves `dist/` over HTTP for local development.

## Building

```
caja build
```

Compiles `main.caja`, runs it once to (re)generate `dist/`, and prints where
the output landed.

## Deploying

`dist/` is a plain directory of static files — point any static file host
(Netlify, GitHub Pages, S3 + CloudFront, nginx, ...) at it.
